    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0102" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 28, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 20th of
                    October, relative to the British steamer Mary, formerly the Alexandra ram, and
                    her supposed connexion with the so-called confederate government, I have the
                    honor to transmit to you herewith copy of a despatch, and of its enclosures,
                    from the governor of New Providence, stating that he has ordered the seizure of
                    the steamer Mary, for violation of the 7th clause of the foreign enlistment
                    act.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d43-a1.xml" xpointer="d43-a1"/>
